title: find_calls

!! `find_calls` MCP Tool

Where a macro, procedure, function or custom widget is called or defined, found through ~TiddlyWiki's own parsers. The editor's find references answers the same question from the same code, see [[LSP Find References]].

!! Parameters

|!Parameter |!Default |!Description |
|`name` |required |the name called; a custom widget keeps its `$`, as in `$my.widget` |
|`filter` |`[all[tiddlers]!is[system]]` |TW filter expression to scope the search |
|`include_system` |`false` |convenience flag for $:/ tiddlers; ignored if `filter` is set |
|`include_definitions` |`true` |also list the `\define`, `\procedure`, `\function` or `\widget` declaring the name |
|`max_total` |`200` |cap on calls plus definitions; a tiddler is listed whole or not at all |

!! Output format

```
<title>
  <line>#<hash> [<forms>]: <line text>
```

The anchor is what `edit_tiddler` takes as `pos`, so a call can be changed in the next step. Forms are `macro`, `macrocall`, `transclude`, `widget`, `filter` and `definition`, and a line holding several calls lists each form once. A footer counts calls, definitions and tiddlers.

!! What counts as a call

Every form listed in [[LSP Find References]]: `<<name>>`, the `$macrocall` and `$transclude` widgets, attribute values, filters, and calls inside definition bodies. A name built at render time cannot be found.

Unlike the editor, the tool answers from the wiki rather than from files, so shadow tiddlers such as the core macros are searched whenever the scope includes them.

!! Direct invocations

```
find_calls(name="list-links")
find_calls(name="list-links", filter="[all[shadows+tiddlers]]")
find_calls(name="$my.widget")
find_calls(name="list-links", include_definitions=false)
```

!! See also

* [[LSP Find References]]: the same answer in the editor
